    "notes": [
      {
        "category": "summary",
        "text": "An update is available for linux-firmware.\nThis update affects Rocky Linux 8.\nA Common Vulnerability Scoring System (CVSS) base score, which gives a detailed severity rating, is available for each vulnerability from the CVE list",
        "title": "Topic"
      },
      {
        "category": "description",
        "text": "The linux-firmware packages contain all of the firmware files that are required by various devices to operate.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* kernel: Reserved fields in guest message responses may not be zero initialized (CVE-2023-31346)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.\n\nThis advisory is provided by Ctrl IQ, Inc for Rocky Linux systems. For more information about CIQ security practices, visit https://ciq.com/security.",
        "title": "Description"
      },
      {
